#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for the snap format and snap.yaml metadata, including "
"package structure, hooks, interfaces, layouts, and desktop files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:8
msgid "The snap format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:10
msgid ""
"ⓘ  This page documents the format of the **built** snaps. See [The snapcraft "
"format](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/project-"
"file/snapcraft-yaml) for more information about the `snapcraft.yaml` file "
"used to build these snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:12
msgid ""
"A snap is a *SquashFS* file carrying content alongside metadata to tell the "
"system how it should be manipulated. When installed, the SquashFS file for "
"the snap is mounted read-only at the following location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:14
msgid "`/snap/<snap name>/<revision>/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:16
msgid ""
"This method delivers fast and extremely predictable installations, with no "
"installation remnants, and no way for a snap's content to be mutated or "
"interfered with. A snap is either installed and available as originally "
"built, or it is not available at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:18
msgid "Applications declared in the snap become commands at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:20
msgid "`/snap/bin/<snap name>[.<app name>]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:22
msgid "The suffix is omitted if `<app name>` matches `<snap name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:24
msgid ""
"That snap command file is not the actual application, but rather a link to "
"the real application under the isolation and confinement rules of the snap's "
"default restricted environment, plus any allowances granted to it via the "
"interface system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:26
msgid "<a name=\"files\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:26
msgid "<a name=\"files\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:26
#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:246
#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:252
#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:260
#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:268
msgid "</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:28
msgid "Setup files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:30
msgid "The following files control the behaviour of a snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:32
msgid "`meta/snap.yaml`: Basic snap details (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:33
msgid "`meta/hooks/`: Hooks called on specific events (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:34
msgid "`meta/gui/icon.{svg,png}`: Icon for the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:35
msgid "`meta/gui/*.desktop`: Desktop files for the snap (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:37
msgid "<h3 id='heading--snapyaml'>snap.yaml</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:39
msgid ""
"Every snap package contains a `meta/snap.yaml` file that holds the basic "
"metadata for the snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:41
msgid "Please take note of this important distinction:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:43
msgid "**snap.yaml** lives inside every snap package, read by snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:44
msgid ""
"**snapcraft.yaml** contains instructions to create a snap package, read by "
"the *snapcraft* command used to build snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:46
msgid ""
"Most of the metadata supported by _snap.yaml_ is optional. In fact, the "
"simplest `snap.yaml` could contain as little as the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:48
msgid ""
"name: simplest\n"
"version: 1.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:53
msgid ""
"An example *snap.yaml* that offers an application to run is still very "
"simple:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:55
msgid ""
"name: simple\n"
"version: 1.0\n"
"apps:\n"
"    hello:\n"
"        command: bin/hello --world\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:63
msgid ""
"The following is the complete specification for the metadata in *snap.yaml*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:65
msgid ""
"# The suggested snap name, constrained to the [a-z0-9] charset and inner\n"
"# dashes. The final name when the snap is installed is defined by the\n"
"# snap-declaration assertion associated with the snap, if any.\n"
"name: <name>\n"
"\n"
"# An optional title for the snap, may contain uppercase letters and spaces.\n"
"title: <title>\n"
"\n"
"# Version of the software packed inside the snap. Has no semantic value\n"
"# in the system (no greater/lower-than rules are ever applied to it).\n"
"version: <version>\n"
"\n"
"# More details about what is contained in the snap.\n"
"summary: <line>\n"
"description: <text>\n"
"\n"
"# License for the snap content, based on SPDX license expressions.\n"
"license: <expression>\n"
"\n"
"# Type of snap, defaults to \"app\". The `core` type has been deprecated.\n"
"type: app | gadget | kernel | base\n"
"\n"
"# List of architectures the snap may run on. Defaults to [all].\n"
"architectures:\n"
"    - all | amd64 | i386 | armhf | ...\n"
"\n"
"# The base snap that defines the underlying filesystem this snap\n"
"# will be assembled on top of.\n"
"base: <name>\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"# A list of features that must be supported by the core for \n"
"# the snap to install. For example, the following sets a requirement for\n"
"# snapd2.38 or later:\n"
"# assumes:\n"
"# - snapd2.38\n"
"assumes:\n"
"    - <feature>\n"
"\n"
"# The epoch this release is intended for. For further details, see:\n"
"# https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/how-to/crafting/manage-"
"data-compatibility/\n"
"# (snapd 2.38+)\n"
"epoch: <value>\n"
"\n"
"# Additional usernames the snap may use. Currently, the only supported\n"
"# values for <name> is '_daemon_' (snapd 2.61+), and the now deprecated\n"
"# 'snap-daemon'. For further details, see:\n"
"# https://snapcraft.io/docs/explanation/snap-development/system-usernames/\n"
"\n"
"system-usernames:\n"
"  <name>: shared\n"
"\n"
"# Alternative form:\n"
"# system-usernames:\n"
"#   <name>:\n"
"#     scope: shared\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"# List of applications (commands, binaries, daemons) in the snap. \n"
"apps:\n"
"\n"
"  <app name>:\n"
"\n"
"      # Path to executable (relative to snap base) and arguments to use\n"
"      # when this application is run.\n"
"      command: <command line>\n"
"\n"
"      # A list of commands to be executed, in order, prior to the `command:` "
"executable\n"
"      # or from within a hook (see below). \n"
"      command-chain: <list of commands>\n"
"\n"
"      # An identifier to a desktop-id within an external appstream file.\n"
"      # See https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/"
"external-package-information/\n"
"      common-id: <desktop file id>\n"
"\n"
"      # Path to a bash snippet to use for tab completion.\n"
"      # (snapcraft 2.33+, snapd 2.30+)\n"
"      # See https://snapcraft.io/docs/explanation/snap-development/tab-"
"completion/\n"
"      completer: <path to file>\n"
"\n"
"      # List of plug names the application is associated with.\n"
"      # When a plug is connected to one of these slots, the application\n"
"      # will be granted the permissions specified for that interface.\n"
"      # If attributes are required, or the plug name does not match the\n"
"      # interface name, more details must be declared under the top-level\n"
"      # \"plugs\" field (see below).\n"
"      plugs:\n"
"          - <plug name>\n"
"\n"
"      # List of slot names this application is associated with.\n"
"      # Same details as described above, but for slots.\n"
"      slots:\n"
"          - <slot name>\n"
"\n"
"      # If daemon is set, the command is a daemon to run as specified.\n"
"      # See systemd documentation for further details.\n"
"      daemon: simple | forking | oneshot | notify\n"
"\n"
"      # Defines whether a freshly installed daemon is started automatically "
"(enabled), \n"
"      # or whether startup is deferred to the snap (disabled). Defaults to "
"enable.\n"
"      install-mode: enable | disable\n"
"     \n"
"      # Controls whether the daemon should be restarted during a snap "
"refresh. Defaults to 'restart'.\n"
"      refresh-mode:  endure | restart\n"
"\n"
"      # Maps a daemon’s sockets to services and activates them.\n"
"      sockets:\n"
"          - <socket name>\n"
"\n"
"      # The mode of a socket in octal, such as `0644`.\n"
"      socket-mode: <mode>\n"
"     \n"
"      # Controls how the daemon should be stopped.  The given signal is sent "
"to the main PID \n"
"      # (when used without -all) or to all PIDs in the process group when "
"the -all suffix is used.\n"
"      stop-mode:  sigterm | sigterm-all | sighup | sighup-all | sigusr1 | "
"sigusr1-all | sigusr2 | sigusr2-all\n"
"\n"
"      # Optional command to stop a daemon.\n"
"      stop-command: <command line>\n"
"\n"
"      # Optional time to wait for daemon to start.\n"
"      start-timeout: <n>ns | <n>us | <n>ms | <n>s | <n>m\n"
"\n"
"      # Optional time to wait for daemon to stop.\n"
"      stop-timeout: <n>ns | <n>us | <n>ms | <n>s | <n>m\n"
"\n"
"      # Optional command to run after daemon stops.\n"
"      post-stop-command: <command line>\n"
"\n"
"      # Condition to restart the daemon under. Defaults to on-failure.\n"
"      # See the systemd.service manual on Restart for details.\n"
"      restart-condition: \\\n"
"          on-failure | on-success | on-abnormal | on-abort | always | never\n"
"\n"
"      # Delay between service restarts. Defaults to unset. \n"
"      # See the systemd.service manual on RestartSec for details.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.36+)\n"
"      restart-delay: <n>ns | <n>us | <n>ms | <n>s | <n>m\n"
"\n"
"      # Service watchdog timeout. For watchdog to work, the application\n"
"      # requires access to systemd notification socket, which can be \n"
"      \n"
"      # declared by listing a daemon-notify plug in the plugs section.\n"
"      # Note, the interface is not auto connected  and needs to be\n"
"      # connected manually.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.33+)\n"
"      watchdog-timeout: <n>ns | <n>us | <n>ms | <n>s | <n>m\n"
"\n"
"      # Command to use to ask the service to reload its configuration.\n"
"      # In the absence of this, when asked to reload  (e.g. via\n"
"      # `snap restart --reload snap.app`) the service is restarted instead.\n"
"      reload-command: <command line>\n"
"\n"
"      # List of applications that are ordered to be started before\n"
"      # the current one. Applications must be part of the same snap.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.31+)\n"
"      before:\n"
"          - <other app name>\n"
"\n"
"      # List of applications that are ordered to be started after\n"
"      # the current one. Applications must be part of the same snap.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.31+)\n"
"      after:\n"
"          - <other app name>\n"
"\n"
"      # The service is activated by a timer, app must be a daemon. See "
"timer\n"
"      # documentation for examples.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.33+)\n"
"      timer: <timer string>\n"
"\n"
"      # Name of the desktop file placed by the application in \n"
"      # $SNAP_USER_DATA/.config/autostart to indicate that application \n"
"      # should be started with the user's desktop session. The application\n"
"      # is started using the app's command wrapper (<name>.<app>) plus\n"
"      # any arguments  present in the Exec=.. line inside the autostart\n"
"      # desktop file.\n"
"      # (snapd 2.32.4+)\n"
"      autostart: <command line>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:246
msgid "<a name=\"hooks\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:246
msgid "<a name=\"hooks\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:248
msgid "Hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:250
msgid ""
"Hooks provide a mechanism for snapd to alert snaps that something has "
"happened, or to ask the snap to provide its opinion about an operation that "
"is in progress. See the topic on {ref}`supported hooks <reference-"
"development-supported-snap-hooks>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:252
msgid "<a name=\"interfaces\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:252
msgid "<a name=\"interfaces\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:254
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:256
msgid ""
"Interfaces allow snaps to communicate or share resources according to the "
"protocol established by the interface. They play an important part in "
"security policy configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:258
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:260
msgid "<a name=\"layouts\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:260
msgid "<a name=\"layouts\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:262
msgid "Layouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:264
msgid ""
"Layouts enable snap developers to modify the execution environment of their "
"snap. They simplify the process of using pre-compiled binaries and libraries "
"that expect to find files and directories outside of locations referenced by "
"$SNAP or $SNAP_DATA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:266
msgid ""
"For more details, see [Snap layouts](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/"
"snapcraft/stable/how-to/crafting/use-layouts/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:268
msgid "<a name=\"desktop-files\"></a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:268
msgid "<a name=\"desktop-files\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:270
msgid "Desktop files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:272
msgid ""
"The `meta/gui/` directory (`snap/gui/` with snapcraft) may contain "
"`*.desktop` files for the snap. These desktop files may contain valid "
"desktop entries from the XDG Desktop Entry Specification version 1.1 with "
"some exceptions listed below. Lines with unknown keys are silently removed "
"from the desktop file on install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:274
msgid "The *Exec=* line must use the following syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:276
msgid "`Exec=<snap name>[.<app name>] [<argument> ...]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:278
msgid ""
"As in the executables contained under `/snap/bin`, the `.<app name>` suffix "
"is omitted if the application name and snap name are the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:280
msgid "For example, assuming this content in `snap.yaml`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:282
msgid ""
"name: http\n"
"version: 1.0\n"
"apps:\n"
"    get:\n"
"        command: bin/my-downloader\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:290
msgid "... the following desktop file would be valid:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:292
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Name=My Downloader\n"
"Exec=http.get %U\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:298
msgid ""
"<h3 id='heading--autostart'>Autostart desktop files<sup><a href='#heading--"
"autostart'>⚓</a></sup></h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:301
msgid ""
"An application may put a desktop file under `$SNAP_USER_DATA/.config/"
"autostart` in order to be automatically started with the user's desktop "
"session. The file is matched with a corresponding application based on the "
"`autostart` property of an app inside `meta/snap.yaml`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:303
msgid ""
"name: my-chat\n"
"version: 1.0\n"
"apps:\n"
"    chat:\n"
"        command: bin/my-chat\n"
"        autostart: my-chat.desktop\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:311
msgid ""
"Assuming `my-chat` has written a file `$SNAP_USER_DATA/.config/autostart/my-"
"chat.desktop` with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:313
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Name=My Chat\n"
"Exec=/usr/bin/my-chat --autostart a b c\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:318
msgid ""
"The *Exec=* line is used to obtain any command line parameters, and the "
"application will be started as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:319
msgid "my-chat.chat --autostart a b c \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:323
msgid "Unsupported desktop keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-snap-format.md:325
msgid ""
"The `DBusActivatable`, `TryExec` and `Implements` keys are currently not "
"supported and will be silently removed from the desktop file on install."
msgstr ""
